Goblin REPL embed
=================

Place this token on its own line in Markdown content or a layout:

    {{{GOBLIN_REPL::EMBED}}}

Sheriff's manifest imports the goblin_repl glam. Its pre-build init action
copies the client and WASM assets; apply_tokens runs late in the page schedule
to emit the embed HTML. A single-page build containing an actual embed also
refreshes missing or outdated assets, without invoking the portal pre/post schedules.

Actions
-------

    goblin_repl::init(pre_ctx)
    goblin_repl::apply_tokens(ctx)

Both actions return the supplied context. The glam never registers its HTML
as a global token, so an earlier Markdown step cannot accidentally expand it
on a later page. Tokens in inline code, fenced code, scripts, and styles stay
literal. Multiple embeds on a page share one WASM initialization and each
has its own session.

Files published with an embed
----------------------------

    /public/js/goblin-repl.js
    /public/wasm/goblin_wasm.js
    /public/wasm/goblin_wasm_bg.wasm

The bundled WASM runtime is shipped as an existing release artifact. Sheriff
does not compile it during builds. After updating the glam, rebuild affected
pages (or the portal) and reload the browser to pick up the corrected embed.

Runtime release
---------------
The browser runtime is Goblin 0.51.26, built from the pinned source commit in
wasm/runtime.json. This is separate from the native executable used by Sheriff.
The REPL displays the version exported by WASM and checks it against its client.
Release URLs include the version so cached older binaries cannot be reused.
A page-only build refreshes existing assets when its runtime manifest changes.

The recorded build.patch enables browser randomness, fixes a WASM-only string
conversion, uses a browser-compatible clock, and exports the CLI version from its Cargo manifest. It does not
change Goblin's language or colon rules. The wrapper crate's 0.1.2 package
version is not the Goblin language version.
